      "writtenOn": "2024-03-20T14:40:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this is right. The PictureShader folds its local matrix into the key context and into the local matrix it creates when calling `image-\u003emakeShader()`, so I think we can say that all picture shaders are covered by the set of image shader combinations and get rid of this class entirely?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 507,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 507,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "b5f50575bb83c70b4dbfb87627df38caea58e167",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a37523ec_7f5d7c6a",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/FactoryFunctions.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 21
      },
      "lineNbr": 507,
      "author": {
        "id": 5230
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-20T16:13:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The PictureShader does go away in https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/827918. However, SkPictureShader::Make wraps an SkPictureShader in a SkLocalMatrixShader. Later, the SkPictureShader is converted into an SkImageShader that is, potentially, wrapped in another SkLocalMatrixShader.",
      "parentUuid": "bb9ffb3a_383198b0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 507,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 507,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "b5f50575bb83c70b4dbfb87627df38caea58e167",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
